[Music]  apartment rents in las vegas  rising rapidly there's a new report by  the nevada state apartment association  showing local rents growing by 18  percent  through the end of the second quarter of  2021 that is compared to last year  the average rent sits at thirteen  hundred dollars now these high prices  high rents concerning many renters which  have seen their  bills go up the past couple of years  kate houston spoke to a local mom about  her rent increase  and digs into why they're going up when  we first moved here it was pretty cheap  nicole jane is a single mom renting a  two-bedroom apartment  her rent has gone up nearly 200 dollars  over the past  three years that did put quite a you  know bit of strain on me these last few  months especially  jane is not alone the nevada state  apartment association  says rent increases have doubled since  the beginning of the year  for workers like jane who have had to  take furlough days and pay cuts during  the pandemic  this is a frustrating situation that was  you know an added  stressor for for me personally because  you know you got a child  i'm making less money than you know i  used to  and plus my rent and other bills went up  so  why are prices going up local property  manager steve hawk says one reason  is extremely high demand and low supply  apartment availability is going down  with the vacancy at only 4.3 percent  that's why we're seeing prices go above  and beyond what locals can  afford most locals cannot afford las  vegas anymore hawks says apartments are  capitalizing on those moving from out of  state who are still saving money with  the local rent increases  they don't care about three or four  hundred bucks they just made a half a  million or a million dollars on their  house in california  they don't care they just want a place  to live and be comfortable the nvsaa  says there are nearly 4 thousand  apartment units under construction in  las vegas  even with more supply on the way jane  says the prices are not realistic  for families try to find someplace else  you know  another area because it's just it's  becoming unaffordable here  kate houston 8 news now now to give you  an idea of the amount of people moving  here clark county's population has  grown by two percent in the past year  that's about 40  000 people that have been moved here in  the past year alone  the nvsaa says that makes it one of the  top 10  fastest growing metro areas in the  country

